=== timeline
scene: castle-night
cast: quill, vampire:thinking
The Countess climbs onto a chair and announces, in a voice that has silenced kings, that it is in fact four thirty-five, that the clocks have been tampered with, and that the dancing will continue. The guests laugh, a little nervously at first, and then the musicians strike up again.

Vampire: Now, Archivist, I believe it is time you told this whole household what has been happening, beginning at the beginning, because everyone has heard the story in pieces.

Quill: Tell it in order. A muddled story protects the person who muddled it.

You lay out your notes on the lectern: the reprinted invitations from Tuesday night, the cancellation letter that reached the farm on Wednesday, your first night in the archive when Pemberton gave you his earwitness account, the upside-down portrait found on your second night, and tonight's clocks.
? RL.5 order : Put the acts of sabotage and your discoveries in the order they happened.
1 The invitations were reprinted for the thirty-first of February.
2 The Marsh farm received a letter cancelling the beet juice.
3 Pemberton told you he had heard a hairy shape near the press.
4 The Countess's portrait was found hanging upside down.
5 Every clock in the castle struck seven during the party.
hint: Follow the days: Tuesday, Wednesday, your first night, your second night, the party.
