=== accuse-final
scene: castle-night
cast: quill, bat:scared, werewolf
The music falls quiet as you walk to the center of the hall, and a hundred faces turn toward you. Pemberton has settled on the highest candelabra, as far from the crowd as possible, and Barnaby has taken off his bow tie and is twisting it anxiously in his paws.

Quill: Make your case from the sources that cannot be talked into anything, the ones made of paper, metal and dust, and leave the echoes out of it. Put them together, and they will speak more clearly than any one of them alone.
? RL.1 : Which set of evidence points most strongly to Pemberton?
+ Curly Bulletin type, lavender paper, and claw marks on the frame
- The festival programme, the almanac, and the parish register
- Pemberton's echo, the Bulletin headline, and Barnaby's fur
- The Chronicle's torch mob, the goat dispute, and the cellar
hint: Which clues connect the fake invitations, the fake letter and the portrait to something only Pemberton uses or can do?
